ksnip-pyqt6 (0.2.2-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Route the layout/table and HTML OCR backends through an optional
    structure script when one is configured. This lets the separate
    ksnip-pyqt6-ocr plugin run PP-StructureV3 in its managed environment
    instead of requiring PaddleOCR in the system Python.
  * Pass KSNIP_OCR_MODE, KSNIP_OCR_LANG, and KSNIP_OCR_FORMULAS to the script,
    and convert HTML table output to Markdown in the core.
  * Keep the direct in-process PP-StructureV3 path for installations that
    have PaddleOCR available in the core interpreter.

 -- wachin <wachin.id@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:35:00 -0500

ksnip-pyqt6 (0.2.2-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Documentation and changelog update. No code changes.
  * Consolidate the OCR fixes from 0.2.2-2 through 0.2.2-4: the main OCR
    action honors the configured backend, the Model Manager reads
    ocr/script_path, optional OCR plugins are discovered through the
    ksnip_py.ocr entry-point group, and the translation fallback preserves
    untranslated plugin strings without aborting on Unicode source text.
  * Document the optional OCR plugin boundary and the Debian main-archive
    constraints in docs/OCR_PLUGIN_ARCHITECTURE.md.
  * The managed PaddleOCR environment, storage-size inspector, legacy-cache
    reporting, and upstream .deb are provided by the separate
    ksnip-pyqt6-ocr package. They are not part of this Debian source package.

 -- wachin <wachin.id@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:20:00 -0500

ksnip-pyqt6 (0.2.2-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the translation fallback for untranslated plugin strings. Returning an
    empty string made plugin dialogs lose their titles and labels; non-ASCII
    tr() source strings could also trigger a UnicodeEncodeError and abort Qt.

 -- wachin <wachin.id@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:30:00 -0500

